                <pb facs="0893" n="875" sameAs="frus:frus1951v06p1/pg875"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Annex] II</seg>
                </opener>
                <p>[Here follows text of the Agreement between the United States of America and
                    Japan for Collective Self-defense initialed February 9 by Messrs. Iguchi and
                    Allison. In it only two changes were made from the draft of February 5, page
                    856. The second sentence of the Preamble now read: “On the coming into force of
                    that Treaty, Japan will not have the means to exercise her inherent right of
                    self-defense because she has been disarmed.” The altered last sentence of
                    numbered paragraph (1) was as follows: “Assistance given at the express request
                    of the Japanese Government to put down large-scale internal riots and
                    disturbances in Japan caused through instigation or intervention <pb facs="0894"
                        n="876" xml:id="pg876"/> by an outside Power or Powers would not be deemed
                    intervention in the internal affairs of Japan.”]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
